  "created": "2026-11-13T12:01:10.047Z",
  "description": "A transactional outbox for .NET on your app's own database (no broker, no Redis): give a domain-event handler `IDurableHandler<T>` and its row is written to an `OutboxMessage` table in the **same transaction** as the change that raised the event, so it is never lost and never fires for a rolled-back change. A background `OutboxProcessor` then runs each handler at-least-once with retries, woken by the save itself. Plain `IEventHandler<T>`s keep running in memory; each handler chooses. Server-side; pairs with Rask.Data and Rask.Cqrs.",
